# A CAPTURED PRESS RELEASE IS EVIDENCE. GIT MUST NOT EDIT IT.
#
# core.autocrlf is true on this machine, so git rewrites line endings on
# checkout for anything it considers text. The extractor's line-ending bug
# was invisible for the whole build because the READER normalised CRLF away;
# a corpus whose bytes change on clone reintroduces exactly that, one layer
# lower, and tests/test_crlf.py would then assert a property of the checkout
# rather than of the wire.
#
# -text: store and check out these files byte for byte, on every machine.
tests/fixtures/releases/** -text
earnings_scraper/state/pending/** -text
